A1  - Nelson, Craig L
A1  - Gary, Ray D
A1  - McIntyre, Iain M
Y1  - 2012//
Y2  - 20120919//
N2  - The highest postmortem metformin concentrations are recorded utilizing a sensitive and specific analytical procedure. The peripheral blood metformin concentration was 240 mg/L, the liver concentration was 240 mg/kg and the gastric concentration was 1,700 mg. Additionally, an antemortem blood sample collected shortly after admission revealed a metformin concentration of 210 mg/L. These data, revealing a liver to peripheral blood ratio of 1.0, provide additional support that metformin is not subject to postmortem redistribution. Intentional self-poisonings with metformin can result in death, despite multiple medical interventions.
